rious for launching two bloody purges, seizing hundreds of women from all over the peninsula to serve as palace entertainers, and appropriating Sungkyunkwan as a personal pleasure ground. His despotic rule provided a stark contrast to the liberal era of his father, and as a much-despised overthrown king, he did not receive a temple name.","wp_description":"King of Joseon from 1495 to 1506","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeonsangun_of_Joseon","image_lead":null,"thumbnail":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%D0%81%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%B3%D1%83%D0%BD_%D0%92%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%A7%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B0_Yeonsangun_of_Jeoson.jpg?width=640","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1495,"display_to":1506}